{
  "case_id": "2017-17-312",
  "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Allon Kedem (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KEDEM: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nAn appellate court must have statutory, as well as constitutional, authority for its decisions, and, here, the Ninth Circuit had neither."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: On your first point, you -- you didn't mention the collateral-order doctrine. What about that? I mean, that's an exception to the 1291 final"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: If they could get mandamus in that case, why can't they ask for mandamus in this case, where, after all, he has been bound without an opportunity -- they bind everybody, arms and legs? Now you can say: Well, he won't win. I don't know. Maybe he will win.\nBut that's your point, they should ask for mandamus?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Allon Kedem (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KEDEM: The preconditions for mandamus are, first of all, that you have to show clear entitlement to the writ, which Respondents can't show, in part, because the district court complied with the Ninth"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is there any reason why we would have to address the question of statutory jurisdiction if there's no Article III jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents' argument is the same restraints that can be applied against me in the detention center, as I'm being transported to the courthouse, being held in a cell within the courthouse, and being transported to the Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How about the voluntary cessation doesn't moot the case"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Their argument is that some of Respondents are reasonably likely to commit future crimes, to get caught, to be prosecuted within the Southern District again, and then to be forced to undergo physical restraints again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: -- just one -- one small question. On a pretrial motion to suppress, where the defendant's in the room, is he in shackles there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the right that they've invoked under Deck versus Missouri is a right about accuracy and fairness, and that's very different from the bail right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: In -- in the latter case, would that fall within the collateral-order doctrine?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Of the -- what are there, 99 districts in the country?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Can you address the question about capable of repetition yet evading review?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF ALLON KEDEM ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents have said that it's just a prediction based on general likelihood, probability, that a future crime will be committed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Kennedy, you have several times asked a question: Couldn't you have this -- this issue come up in the context of a suppression ruling?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is that -- is that five-point restraints?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can you say -- I don't know -- but can you say if the government would -- I don't want to put cooperate, that's too strong -- but at least would not oppose an effort in any of those 150 districts by a defense attorney's organization to try to challenge this policy, either through, as you suggested, an Ex parte Young proceeding or, as you also suggested, an ordinary appeal where they haven't waived the right to appeal and it says explicitly like reserving the -- the suppression motion, we reserve the right to challenge the restraint motion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-312",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22a1180f23818185a7056918522c93f0b58e1991f279487ce67c1592497a6ce8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22a1180f2381-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
